# symbolic SATO template
# family: Mexico Store (MEXICO-ONLY flag + mitemdet/mitemhdr) / 4.5x3 / automatic (PLC only --
# Mexico has no manual-entry print path at all, confirmed in dtlbl067.p's GetItem procedure)
# ported from c:\Workspace\southalr\dtlbl066n.i's S86-engine branch only (the plain 85x/85R
# branch and the "NON SUPPORTED PRINTER STYLE" fallback are not ported -- same S86-first scope
# as the rest of this port; see project memory feature_mexico_label_research_20260923).
#
# Dispatched from SatoTemplateResolver when payload.IsMexicoItem is true -- checked before the
# LabelTypeCode/CustomerChar family branches, matching dtplc067.p's GenSingleLabel: Mexico is a
# hard fork (its own case-statement `return`s immediately), not a shared branch with feature
# flags, so this template shares nothing with lt_retail_45x3/lt04_default_45x3/lt_default_45x3.
#
# Known gaps/simplifications (flagged, not oversights):
#  - Company name/address/body-type description (prt-company-name/addr1/addr2/made-in/
#    prt-body-desc) have no data source in this port (no mitemhdr.mih-body-code lookup table
#    equivalent exists) -- placeholder Spanish text below, real content pending a data source.
#  - "Lot:" is NOT a real lot number -- see ThermalLabelPayload.MexicoLotCode's doc comment.
#  - The internal I-2-of-5 case barcode (prt-I2of5) is not ported (same SAP-item-master-gap
#    class as CrossOver/F&D's sapitemhdr dependencies -- no case-shipping data source here).
#  - "Color" + apply-type suffix is hardcoded to ":" (automated-line marker) since Mexico has
#    no manual print path for the ";" (non-automated) variant to ever occur.

